    "conflict_risks": "MealPlanItemIndex (not ItemIndex) is the canonical name; any downstream bead that references ItemIndex for meal-plan use will need updating. No other active file-scope conflicts detected.",
    "design_decisions": "1. load-mutate-serialise-write pattern confirmed clean across all mutation paths. 2. MealPlanItemIndex name (not ItemIndex) is correct per collision-avoidance rationale documented in architecture.md. 3. .disabled() on SwiftUI alert button is silently ignored \u2014 functional guard in handleCreate() preserves correctness but UX feedback is lost. 4. Navigation destination wired to full MealPlanDetailView (not a stub Text), which is correct for v1. 5. deletePlan() uses parentURL (derived, non-bookmarked) for security scope \u2014 inconsistent with loadPlan() which uses folderURL directly; likely works due to iOS inherited scope but pattern should be corrected.",
    "test_coverage_notes": "MealPlanParserTests: comprehensive \u2014 parse, serialise, round-trip, removeItem including all three guard clauses, free-text and comment items. MealPlanFilesTests: covers plansURL idempotency, discover filter/sort, displayName, read/write round-trip, missing-file nil return. MealPlanDetailViewTests: view instantiation, all three row types, swipe-delete persistence (single item, last item, multi-block), unique recipe count deduplication, block filter correctness and case-insensitivity. MealPlansViewTests: view instantiation, recipe count calculation, name sanitization, create/discover/duplicate-detection flow. Gap: block filter tests use simplified URL path logic (no ./ stripping, no extension stripping) that diverges from the view's recipeDisplayName(for:) implementation.",
    "known_limitations": "1. .disabled() is silently ignored on SwiftUI alert buttons \u2014 Create button always appears enabled even with empty input. handleCreate() guard prevents actual creation. 2. deletePlan() brackets FileManager.removeItem with startAccessingSecurityScopedResource() on a derived URL (not a bookmark); relies on iOS inherited access from the top-level scope. 3. Shopping list generation from meal plan is stubbed \u2014 'Coming in a future update' alert. 4. Block filter tests exercise simplified filtering logic that doesn't cover the ./prefix stripping branch in recipeDisplayName(for:)."
